cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or analysis, please cite it as below."
title: "twostep: E2SFCA Accessibility to OB/GYN Subspecialists in the Contiguous United States"
abstract: >-
  Standalone analysis and manuscript for national travel-time accessibility to the
  seven ABOG-certified obstetric and gynecologic subspecialties across the
  contiguous United States, 2013 to 2023, using an Enhanced Two-Step Floating
  Catchment Area (E2SFCA) method on road-network isochrones with a mass-conserving
  demand allocation and a Spatial Access Ratio (SPAR). Extracted from the
  isochrones pipeline so the accessibility paper builds and reproduces
  independently.
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-08-29
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mufflyt/twostep"
url: "https://github.com/mufflyt/twostep"
authors:
  - family-names: Muffly
    given-names: Tyler
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2044-1693"
    email: tyler.muffly@dhha.org
    affiliation: "Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, Denver Health"
keywords:
  - E2SFCA
  - two-step floating catchment area
  - spatial accessibility
  - SPAR
  - OBGYN subspecialties
  - isochrones
  - drive-time access
  - health disparities
  - reproducible research
# The papers this implementation REPRODUCES and is tested against, not
# background reading. Each has a fixture or a variant in the test suite:
# Luo & Qi supplies the published weight sets and a worked example the suite
# reproduces exactly; Delamater supplies M2SFCA, which a mutation-corpus mutant
# is killed by; McGrail supplies the Gaussian decay variant used in the
# specification curve; Wan et al. supplies the Spatial Access Ratio.
